cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "hazardtrace: STPA control-structure hazard analysis as a machine-checkable artifact"
abstract: >-
  Reads a declared System-Theoretic Process Analysis from YAML - losses,
  hazards, system-level constraints, the control structure, unsafe control
  actions in the four STPA classes, loss scenarios, mitigations and evidence -
  and computes what is missing from it: enumeration gaps over the control
  action by class grid, hazards with no constraint, constraints with no
  requirement, unsafe control actions with no loss scenario, loss scenarios
  with no mitigation, mitigations with no evidence, and cited requirement and
  test identifiers that do not resolve against the repository. Deterministic,
  with no learned component. It checks the completeness of a declared argument
  and evaluates no argument's correctness or adequacy. Research-grade; not
  flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational aerospace use,
  and it discharges no safety obligation.
